Stateless Address Auto-configuration (SLAAC) :

		* Hosts uses RS/RA messages to learn the IPv6 prefix of the local link (ie: 2001:db8::/64), then automatically generate an IPv6 		  address

		* Using the IPv6 address ipv6 address prefix/prefix-length eui-64 , you need to manually enter the prefix
				       Network	<-------|	|---> ex. /64

		* using the IPv6 address autoconfig command, you dont need to enter the prefix.  the device uses NDP to learn the prefix used on the 		  local link

		* The device will use EUI-64 to generate the interface ID, or it will be randomly generated (depending on the device/maker)

Duplicate Address Detection (DAD) :

		* One final point about NDP

		* Duplicate Address Dectection allows hosts to check if other devices on the local link are using the same IPv6 address

		* Any time an IPv6 enable interface initializes, it perform DAD

		* DAD uses two messages you leaned earlier: NS and NA

		* The host will send an NS to its own IPv6 address. if it doesnt get a reply, it knows the address is unique
	
		* if it gets a reply it means another host on the network is already using the address

IPv6 Static Routing :
		
		* IPv6 routing works the same as IPv4 routing

			- uses seperate routing tables as Ipv4

		* Ipv4 routing is enable bby default
			
			- Ipv6 is disable by default , unicast routing to enable.

		* If Ipv6 routing is disabled, the router will be able to send and receive Ipv6 traffic but will not route IPv6 traffic

		* Connected network route is automatically added for each connected network

		* Local host route is automatically added for each address configured on the router	

		* Routes for link-local addresses are not added to the routing table

		* Route Types :

			- Directly Attached ( Static Route) : only exit interface is specified
			
				# ipv6 route destination/prefix-length exit-int

			- Recursive Static Route : only the next host is specified

				# ipv6 route destination/prefix-length next-hop

			- Fully Specified static route : Both the exit int and next hop are specified

				# ipv6 route destination/prefix-length exit-interface next-hop

			- Default Route 

				# ipv6 route ::/0 2001:db8:0:23::1

				





						








					